  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Six charges are placed around a regular hexagon of side length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;as shown in the figure. Five of them have charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math>, and the remaining one has charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>. The perpendicular from each charge to the nearest hexagon side passes through the center <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>&nbsp;of the hexagon and is bisected by the side.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0012_0f8683ea98d8.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 226px;\" /></p><p>Which of the following statement(s) is(are) correct in SI units?</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<p>When <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi></math>, the magnitude of the electric field at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> is zero.</p>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "When <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>q</mi></math>, the magnitude of the electric field at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msub><mo>&#8712;</mo><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>.",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "When <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi></math>, the potential at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>&#960;</mi><msub><mo>&#8712;</mo><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>.",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "When <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>q</mi></math>, the potential at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>&#960;</mi><msub><mi>&#1013;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>.",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A",
    "B",
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0012_708b456baa29.png\" style=\"width: 179px; height: 186px;\" />​​​​​​​</p><p>The given arrangements of the charges also form a regular hexagon with side length equal to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>a</mi></math></p><p>When <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi></math>, the situation is symmetric</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&rArr;</mo></math> Electric field at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>&nbsp;would be zero.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&rArr;</mo><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced></math> is correct.</p><p>When <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>q</mi></math>, we can think of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. Therefore, the magnitude of the electric field will be equivalent to that if only&nbsp;charge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi></math>&nbsp;is kept at the the bottom point. Hence,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&pi;</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><msup><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&pi;</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>&pi;</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&rArr;</mo><mfenced><mi>B</mi></mfenced></math> is correct</p><p>For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi></math>, potential at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&times;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&pi;</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&pi;</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>&pi;</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&rArr;</mo><mfenced><mi>C</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is correct</p><p>For&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&times;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&pi;</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&pi;</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>&pi;</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&rArr;</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>D</mi></mfenced></math>is not correct.</p>"
  }
